/// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
///  THE CLUB FEE LEDGER (#372, P48)
/// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
///
/// The platform charges each club a percentage of the court price on its
/// ONLINE bookings that were played (status COMPLETED). The owner invoices
/// the club from a monthly statement, outside playerz.
///
/// ═══ A LEDGER, NOT A RECOMPUTE ═══
///
/// A statement summed live from `booking` would change under the owner's feet:
/// a new fee percentage, a renamed court or a later status change would all
/// rewrite a month that may already be on an invoice. So the fee is WRITTEN
/// DOWN once, when the booking becomes COMPLETED, with everything the
/// statement shows copied onto the line, and a database trigger refuses any
/// UPDATE or DELETE.
///
/// ═══ A CORRECTION IS A NEW LINE ═══
///
/// A booking can stop being "played" after it was charged: staff mark a
/// COMPLETED booking as a no-show. That writes a REVERSAL: the same booking,
/// the charge's price and fee negated, in the statement month the correction
/// was MADE. Never in the original month, which may be invoiced already; the
/// next statement then carries the credit. A statement is the sum of its
/// lines, so this needs no special case anywhere.
///
/// No foreign keys, on purpose: the ledger must outlive the booking, the
/// court and the venue it names, as `audit_entry` outlives its actors.
enum ClubFeeLineKind {
  /// The booking was played: the fee on its price, or 0 in the free period.
  CHARGE
  /// The charge above, undone (a no-show marked after completion).
  REVERSAL
}

model ClubFeeLine {
  id       String @id @default(cuid())
  tenantId String

  bookingId String
  kind      ClubFeeLineKind

  /// What the statement shows, as it was when the line was written.
  venueId        String
  venueName      String
  resourceId     String
  courtName      String
  bookingStartTs DateTime @db.Timestamptz(3)

  /// `YYYY-MM` at the club (Europe/Sofia): the booking's start for a CHARGE,
  /// the moment of the correction for a REVERSAL. A string, so a month is one
  /// equality and the time-zone arithmetic happens once, in code, when the
  /// line is written (src/lib/billing/club-fee.ts).
  statementMonth String

  /// The court price: the server quote stored on the booking. Negative on a REVERSAL.
  priceCents Int
  /// The rate in force when the line was written, in basis points (12.5% = 1250).
  feeBps     Int
  /// Whether the booking was played inside the club's free period; the fee is then 0.
  freePeriod Boolean
  /// Rounded half-up to the cent, per line. Negative on a REVERSAL.
  feeCents   Int
  currency   String

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)

  /// One charge and at most one reversal per booking: what makes writing a
  /// line idempotent (INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING).
  @@unique([bookingId, kind])
  /// A club's statement for a month.
  @@index([tenantId, statementMonth])
  /// The platform's overview: every club's lines for a month.
  @@index([statementMonth])
  @@map("club_fee_line")
}
